; Probe 1 of the caret arc: `(^Name: T): (body)` reparents every body edge
; under Name's own node id (AGENTS.md:107).
;
; Reads rc=0 once `valid_atom` carries the `^` arm, as THREE top-level terms:
; a form, the atom `:`, a form. `(edge): (body)` is not one form; the infix
; colon at `src/_0_read/_4_expand.rs:169-174` only fires inside a form, so the
; AGENTS.md:105 spelling `((Name: T): (body))` is the one that groups.
;
; Compiles rc=1, `expected_call` on the bare top-level `:` at reader_node 8.
; Even once it groups it does not compile. Three throw sites, all outside this
; lane's ownership:
;   src/_2_lower/_1_forms.rs:70   `bind_form` takes exactly 3 items, so the
;                                 after-form `(: User greet (<- ...))` is not
;                                 a bind and lowers to nothing.
;   src/_2_lower/_2_declare.rs:339 `lower_edge_bind` answers `expected_bind`
;                                 for a bare rule nested in `(* ...)`.
;   src/_2_lower/_2_declare.rs:288 every edge owned by the product counts
;                                 toward arity, so a namespace edge beside the
;                                 closed tuple has no shape.
; A labelled rule is `undeclared_relation(<-)` besides, per AGENTS.md:92.

(^User: (* (: a text))): (
  (: greet (<- (greet ?User ?Salutation) (User ?User ?Name) (str.cons "hi " ?Name ?Salutation)))
)
